<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh Feb copper output falls 5.2 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Kazakh Feb copper output falls 5.2 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan produced 18,521 tonnes of copper in February, down 5.2 percent from the 19,533 tonnes it produced in January, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It gave the following figures for metals production (all figures in tonnes).</p>
<p> KAZAKH METALS OUTPUT  Feb 97	 Jan 97	 Jan-Feb 97</p>
<p> Copper		    18,521	 19,533	   38,054</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change    -5.2	  -10.1	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change   -22.2	  -20.2	    -21.2</p>
<p> Zinc			14,172	 14,027	   28,199</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change    +1.0	   -8.4	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change   +13.1	  +10.3	    +11.7</p>
<p> Lead			 3,196	  3,392	    6,588</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change    -5.8	  -46.8	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change   -39.9	  -39.8	    -39.8</p>
<p> Bauxite		  277,000	181,600	  458,600</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change   +52.5	  -40.3	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change   +46.6	  -27.6	     +4.3</p>
<p> Alumina		   86,246	 91,955	  178,201</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change    -6.2	   -2.1	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change    +3.2	   +2.7	     +3.0</p>
<p> Titanium		   1,500	  1,500	    3,000</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change     0.0	  +23.8	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change   +63.4	  +66.5	    +64.9</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
